+# Add t and use it to check PlaceBlock arguments
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker (`osyrisrblx/t`, pinned to
+  `=3.1.1`, the latest version on the Wally index) to `pesde.toml`. Like our other packages, it
+  comes from Wally through pesde and links at `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`.
+- Switches the `PlaceBlock` handler in `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau` from
+  hand-written argument checks to one `t.tuple` check. Later remotes can follow the same pattern.
+- Adds t to the package table in `README.md`.
+
+## Before you test: install the package
+
+**`pesde.lock` is not updated in this PR**, and `roblox_packages` doesn't have t yet. Until you
+install it, `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)` fails, `BlockPlacement` errors on startup,
+and `luau-lsp analyze` can't resolve the module. From the project root:
+
+```sh
+pesde install
+rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts
+```
+
+Then **commit the updated `pesde.lock`** to this branch so CI and other contributors get the same
+version.
+
+## The checks are the same as before
+
+| Check before | Check now |
+|---|---|
+| `typeof(blockTypeName) ~= "string"` | `t.string` (tuple index 1) |
+| `typeof(position) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` (tuple index 2) |
+| `position ~= position` (NaN) | `notNaN`, combined with `t.Vector3` via `t.intersection` |
+| block type exists in `BlockTypes.ByName` | unchanged |
+| rate limit, character/root part, `Y < 0`, occupied cell, reach | unchanged |
+
+Note: `t.Vector3` is only `t.typeof("Vector3")`. It **doesn't** reject a Vector3 with a NaN
+component (unlike `t.number`, which does reject NaN). That's why the handler keeps the NaN check
+as a small custom check. Like before, extra arguments after the position are ignored.
+
+## Testing
+
+Already run on this branch: `stylua --check src` and `selene src` both pass.
+`luau-lsp analyze` wasn't run, because it needs the package installed (see above).
+
+After installing, in Studio (Play):
+
+1. Placing a valid block type at a reachable position still places a block.
+2. In the client command bar, send bad input with
+   `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer(...)`. None of these should place a block or
+   cause a server error:
+   - `FireServer(123, Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))` (name isn't a string)
+   - `FireServer("Brick", "0,4,0")` (position isn't a Vector3)
+   - `FireServer("Brick", Vector3.new(0/0, 4, 0))` (NaN component)
+   - `FireServer("NotABlock", Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))` (unknown block type)
+   - `FireServer("Brick")` (missing position)
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
